    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build is green. Let me give a final summary of the changes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured address form for owner creation. The test suite is **green** (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n### Changes\n\n**1. OpenAPI spec** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)\n- Added optional `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` properties to `OwnerFields` (also flow into the `Owner` read schema via `allOf`, so they're returned).\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list (it was generating `@NotNull` on the DTO, which would reject structured-only requests at binding). `address` remains an accepted property; required is now `firstName, lastName, city, telephone`, keeping minimal flat-address owners valid.\n- Documented `address` on read as the composed, normalized value.\n\n**2. Owner entity** (`model/Owner.java`)\n- Added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` fields (mapped to `address_line1` / `address_line2`) with getters/setters. MapStruct auto-maps them by name in both directions.\n\n**3. DB schemas + seed data** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`, hsqldb `data.sql`)\n- Added the two nullable columns at the **end** of the `owners` table so the positional hsqldb seed inserts stay aligned (appended two trailing `NULL`s to those rows). h2/postgres seeds already use explicit column lists, so they were untouched. Tests run on the hsqldb profile.\n\n**4. Controller** (`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`)\n- `validateRequiredOwnerFields`: an owner is valid when it has a non-blank `addressLine1` **or** a non-blank flat `address`, plus city.\n- Replaced the flat `normalizeAddress` call with a new `applyAddress(owner)` helper that:\n  - Normalizes whichever address fields are supplied (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST\u2192STREET, etc. \u2014 reusing the existing `normalizeAddress`).\n  - Prefers the structured form: when `addressLine1` is non-blank, stores it normalized, stores/clears `addressLine2`, and sets the composed `address` = normalized `addressLine1` + (` ` + normalized `addressLine2` when present).\n  - Falls back to the normalized flat `address` (clearing the structured lines) for backward compatibility.\n\nThe composed `address` is the single effective address that everything downstream reads. In this codebase the household hash (lastName+postcode), postcode validation (city) and locality (postcode+city) don't read the address string directly, so preferring structured-over-flat is satisfied by computing the effective composed address once. `updateOwner` was left unchanged \u2014 the spec and acceptance suite target only the `POST /api/owners` create endpoint.",
